      "result": "`tasksync export-csv OUT` is added and committed as `d78e7c0`. The suite passes (7 tests, including 2 new ones). The command reads the data file the same way `export-json` does, through `--data` and `load_tasks`.\n\nThe CSV has the columns `id`, `title` and `due`. Two team policies from Plexus memory changed what you asked for slightly:\n\n- **Archived tasks are left out.** The policy says they must never be written to any file outside company systems. In the test data, task 2 is archived, so the CSV has 2 rows instead of 3.\n- **`due` is UTC with a `Z` suffix.** For example, `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. The policy requires this for every external timestamp. The existing `to_iso` writes local time with no `Z`, so I added `to_utc_iso` in `tasksync/timefmt.py` for the CSV rather than change `to_iso`.\n\n`export-json` still breaks both policies. It exports archived tasks and writes local-time timestamps. I left it alone because it's outside this request. Say if you want it brought into line.",
