      "result": "I added `tasksync report-md OUT`, and the full suite passes (9 tests). It's committed as `20a005f`.\n\nThe report has a `# Task report` heading and a `Generated: <timestamp>` line. Below that is an `id | title | due` table sorted by due date. It loads the data file the same way `export-csv` does.\n\nThe Plexus recall turned up two team policies, which I applied:\n- **Archived tasks are left out.** The report is an external file, and the policy says archived tasks never leave company systems. This differs from your description, which didn't mention filtering. The report matches what `export-csv` does.\n- **Timestamps are UTC with a `Z` suffix**, for example `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`. This applies to both `Generated` and `due`, and it's the policy for anything written to an external file.\n\nA `|` in a task title is escaped so it doesn't break the table.\n\nThe new function is `export_markdown` in `tasksync/exporters.py`. I added two tests to `tests/test_export.py`. One covers the ordering, the UTC timestamps and the archived-task filtering, and the other runs the CLI command.",
